 ticket files and a `.gitkeep`\nare still inside it, and that the live tree's source list holds no `.git`\nsegment. It also runs a mutation: with \".git\" removed, the pack is swept again.\nReverting the T-3069 line by hand makes the self-test fail.\n\nChangelog: none, because this only changes the gate and visitors see nothing.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-23T16:15:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/commit/ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3/comments","author":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8710b89815b18ae308521649423541d228ce9d38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/8710b89815b18ae308521649423541d228ce9d38","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/commit/8710b89815b18ae308521649423541d228ce9d38"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":2,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":2,"commits":[{"sha":"e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454","node_id":"C_kwDOUoK9jtoAKGUxMzIxOWM3MDZiNWJmYjdkNjVjNzk1ZTdjMDRiN2JkYjg0YWM0NTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Kevin Haas","email":"kevinroberthaas@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-23T18:25:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-23T18:25:04Z"},"message":"T-3025: Glessner's roofs ruled red tile; the prints' grey is not shown (#1245)\n\nThe roofs, the stable cupola's pyramid included, read slate-grey in every print\nwhere the record lays red baked, unglazed terracotta tile. Ruled on the two\nwritten sources: Glessner's 1923 description of the house as built (\"The roofs\nare of red baked tiles, unglazed\", re-read in the HABS transcription, data\np. 13) and HABS's 1963 survey, which found terracotta under tar (data p. 21)\nand so excludes slate. Every print is monochrome: the 1963-65 HABS prints show\nthe tar, and the record's red tile reduced to luminance through the Cornell\ncamera reads the same slate-grey. Nothing in the record moves; nothing is\nrebaked. The three match records' covering items close as `not shown` with\nthe ruling.\n\nThe Cornell print's courses read about 6.4 in against the model's 5 in\n(three column bands, ratio 1.28); that is a module question, filed as T-3072.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d87466d5aeda84c30a60f6cf14dbebaef00ffbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/git/trees/5d87466d5aeda84c30a60f6cf14dbebaef00ffbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/git/commits/e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq26aACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAwoQAEneNtfWKUguiao4JGRBjh24\ngcSsrExMqhj2/ps6Dbr9hu8FJeSkffxO7OTKA5rvXSdzz18VFJVfESKhgTADfEM1\n7xfRXhsKuRZo+m9zJ2v6VjkEMtgUSXTjHgBRuL/rG3Qi1NrVSIiOdigX2+YMrI32\nGougvTDE9sNhBQzToPeageJvlURwyLgwukLXSjKcaj7v/J3Nt6m0QB7JbZbR+JNL\nZZds7ezioCINOO6R5gJZJaEC0cuMQZx3zt+obs/QvPkWL9GrPv9kIW2ofY1oVuXw\nqyB0rvCIckLhaYwvh16tBgapCIj8dsZSmf6mQ7r99vuhCdHoPdH9zwlDWunus/J5\nINOa+cyK2HTsnRIUg9awQRyuFBRxTldR6faG9G1oSi8sTxHMLOPmvczq+UizCNpI\nEZKu0dbsdMcHHtOLFNaLWFE8hKag6834wr5b5tKjX210W4LxcXjJMaumXTR9/3X/\nH++sbJyY+Z6E4jRwnMdnX6b4sZyGXoZer54BaJX1punPeXAJwSUQ2T7Gi+W3mVNc\nugaulg80Xu+BJSEt/jOwyOYAea8meQSIiwA7XAZOC2Q5w4qnU4K3CgTbIIPnfSK8\nTbVCK5v74GUshVpYtVspFurb9fOi5JhgvFlj8THydR9Rra1SWLFwIF/8neZZDUu1\nLWMYGHbqtd/gqE3s7gv6\n=1YGj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5d87466d5aeda84c30a60f6cf14dbebaef00ffbc\nparent ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3\nauthor Kevin Haas <kevinroberthaas@gmail.com> 1792779904 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792779904 +0000\n\nT-3025: Glessner's roofs ruled red tile; the prints' grey is not shown (#1245)\n\nThe roofs, the stable cupola's pyramid included, read slate-grey in every print\nwhere the record lays red baked, unglazed terracotta tile. Ruled on the two\nwritten sources: Glessner's 1923 description of the house as built (\"The roofs\nare of red baked tiles, unglazed\", re-read in the HABS transcription, data\np. 13) and HABS's 1963 survey, which found terracotta under tar (data p. 21)\nand so excludes slate. Every print is monochrome: the 1963-65 HABS prints show\nthe tar, and the record's red tile reduced to luminance through the Cornell\ncamera reads the same slate-grey. Nothing in the record moves; nothing is\nrebaked. The three match records' covering items close as `not shown` with\nthe ruling.\n\nThe Cornell print's courses read about 6.4 in against the model's 5 in\n(three column bands, ratio 1.28); that is a module question, filed as T-3072.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-23T18:25:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/commit/e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454/comments","author":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/commit/ea22b3c3055d0c6d40f213273138103fbc98cee3"}]},{"sha":"e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","node_id":"C_kwDOUoK9jtoAKGUzYmFmOTMyM2IwNmExZmI2NmQzYTUwNmI3NDMwZjlmMTBjZDc4NTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Kevin Haas","email":"kevinroberthaas@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-23T18:26:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-23T18:26:16Z"},"message":"T-3063: 1811 Prairie's south gable falls behind its tall stack to a level coped wall head (#1248)\n\nBehind the tall stack, the 1888 plate's coping runs level at about 10.95 m back to the\nfront block's rear wall, into the flank's vanishing point (u 5.9 at 10.96 m, u -0.3 at\n10.98 m through the T-2541 camera), and the Chicagology print draws the same: a short\nsteep fall from the stack, then one level line past the second stack. Neither shows\nany roof over it. The build's coping instead fell down the 22.4-degree rear slope.\n\nK01's gable roof learns `rear_fall` (coped ends only): the rear slope falls from the\nridge at its pitch to a flat deck, and the coped parapet falls with it to a level wall\nhead, its coping's top at wall_head_m, its head running head_back_m behind the ridge.\n1811 takes 10.95 m, the street's 61.2 degrees and 0.1 m. Rendered, the coping stands\nwithin about 4 px of the plate from x 533 to 566 and the second stack's top at y 394\nagainst 393-396. Every other K01 house re-emits byte-identical (k01_emit --check);\nthe 31 meshes that read K01's generators are re-emitted for their manifest inputs.\n\nThe range behind the block steps down to about 8.6 m in both pictures, where the\nbuild carries it at 11.4 m: T-3077.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34f7a55ed9e069de4d9a49df2a7b7537e79c23b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/git/trees/34f7a55ed9e069de4d9a49df2a7b7537e79c23b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/git/commits/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq26bICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjYsQAGr1xIEw2h2Uobce/jDNI9LF\nVFIbRqaAp7RkHdV3iASmidvmokkwgwTwj2t/KhEUQD2VFMpdaLkyMa5GUFx9gzMm\nKHmq0aRbDEbfuQdRIPwildS/X44cBP8sUy5YR5gZPjJDrTB1TXNCIRHJoisjwNmt\n5M/PBOqlO574XrnhdPPDAEc3T4wF2ozotBProVMSQTOAK4YEwmQuxXqa+2owu3HZ\n4qiCoLj7JBhR6/gJa4xZFzIsnsnXcsYLGeBAoP2Ury4JXxhZnur2JKbGjuUkJPkb\nCeXwMenIygt6svRAC2P1zRKEOccH0ZUQYA1BcqoR7qFztwKRdXZO4r8h+9vxcOL2\nJ7C/8bxl5bPJwDdbm1amkvLK353PCcp7Ypddf0sPQAfI2nFHFPmhBvDazBMJO402\nzKdq3Q/LbsC1+0U89tNl7JqmFR/ASpfwLJX8bBIwr++eRaVLzgaJi0Wp+MHd7FlJ\nwvQqyvGfb9pca4XvStiJcqIaXi7CbjOUIN58W5M5mbu5ij6phLIdKxI5UyX2BoWp\n4/EK4dvRhfWy3iQYqWuZhZ16EqAXGfglUBnQhFEE8BkLo+2Sqmvo4K3Z35kZxyeD\nypRvNs5ioJa43tuA+/bLig8QxUxLmgnOyLX4tnOnytwUMUzWSbTMJG8K/D45HxJN\nMTNLvbuCFO55HpONn/aK\n=DYIW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 34f7a55ed9e069de4d9a49df2a7b7537e79c23b9\nparent e13219c706b5bfb7d65c795e7c04b7bdb84ac454\nauthor Kevin Haas <kevinroberthaas@gmail.com> 1792779976 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792779976 +0000\n\nT-3063: 1811 Prairie's south gable falls behind its tall stack to a level coped wall head (#1248)\n\nBehind the tall stack, the 1888 plate's coping runs level at about 10.95 m back to the\nfront block's rear wall, into the flank's vanishing point (u 5.9 at 10.96 m, u -0.3 at\n10.98 m through the T-2541 camera), and the Chicagology print draws the same: a short\nsteep fall from the stack, then one level line past the second stack. Neither shows\nany roof over it. The build's coping instead fell down the 22.4-degree rear slope.\n\nK01's gable roof learns `rear_fall` (coped ends only): the rear slope falls from the\nridge at its pitch to a flat deck, and the coped parapet falls with it to a level wall\nhead, its coping's top at wall_head_m, its head running head_back_m behind the ridge.\n1811 takes 10.95 m, the street's 61.2 degrees and 0.1 m. Rendered, the coping stands\nwithin about 4 px of the plate from x 533 to 566 and the second stack's top at y 394\nagainst 393-396. Every other K01 house re-emits byte-identical (k01_emit --check);\nthe 31 meshes that read K01's generators are re-emitted for their manifest inputs.\n\nThe range behind the block steps down to about 8.6 m in both pictures, where the\nbuild carries it at 11.4 m: T-3077.\n\nCo-authored-by: polecat-steward <steward@polecat.live>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-23T18:26:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/commit/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/commits/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/comments","author":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://ap