ts top edge stands at (528, 374-380) px just clear of the stack and at (572, 485) px at the block's rear wall, which the camera puts on the wall's plane (v 10.4) at u 5.9, 10.96 m and u -0.3, 10.98 m, a line running into the flank's vanishing point; the second stack stands on it, 26-35 px over it. The print, from further south-west, draws the same: a short steep fall from the tall stack, then a long coping line back past the second stack to a step down at the block's rear. Neither picture shows any roof over that coping, where the plain 22.4-degree rear slope stood the coping 0.5-1.4 m higher and its own covering over it near the ridge. So `rear_fall`: the coping's top level at 10.95 m from the rear wall to where the fall meets the deck; the parapet's head runs on only 0.1 m behind the ridge (the plate's coping has already fallen at u 5.9, just behind the stack), and the rear slope falls from the ridge at the street's own 61.2 degrees to a flat deck 0.38 m under the coping (K05's 0.3 m upstand and the 0.08 m coping) running back to the rear wall. The head's level height (10.95 m) is read; the fall's pitch and the deck are inferred (no picture sees behind the coping), the street's pitch the plainest choice; L-k01-1811-rear-fall-3063.\"\n         },\n         \"dormer\": {\n           \"value\": {"},{"sha":"c1e279cb57b2855464fa82500f5d87c7ad1ecb99","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/LIBERTIES.md","status":"modified","additions":30,"deletions":0,"changes":30,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FLIBERTIES.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FLIBERTIES.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FLIBERTIES.md?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -31678,3 +31678,33 @@ Levy's print and 1955.\n **Review:** `docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/wheeler_house_1812_prairie/c1955_front-side-by-side.jpg`,\n `docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/wheeler_house_1812_prairie/levy_front-side-by-side.jpg`.\n **Recorded:** 2026-10-23 (T-3034).\n+\n+### L-k01-1811-rear-fall-3063 — 1811 Prairie's roof behind the south gable falls steeply to a flat deck under a level coped wall head\n+\n+**Decision:** behind the tall stack, 1811 Prairie's south wall (K01's `north`) is built as a\n+coped parapet whose coping's top runs LEVEL at 10.95 m back to the front block's rear wall, and\n+the roof under it falls from the ridge at the street's 61.2 degrees to a flat deck 0.38 m under\n+the coping, where T-3050 had a plain rear slope falling at 22.4 degrees to the rear wall's eave and\n+the coping following it down. The kit learns it (`gable_roof.rear_fall`, coped ends only); every\n+other K01 house re-emits byte-identical.\n+**What is read, not invented.** Through the T-2541 camera on the 1888 Inland Architect plate\n+(`inland_architect_1888_10_ames_residence`): the coping's top edge just clear of the tall stack at\n+(528, 374-380) px and at the block's rear wall at (572, 485) px, which the camera puts on the\n+wall's plane at u 5.9, 10.96 m and u -0.3, 10.98 m, a line running into the flank's vanishing\n+point; the second stack's top 26-35 px over it. The Chicagology print (`cgn-1811-coleman-ames-photo`,\n+rights unknown, read in the image store's display copy and not committed) draws the same from\n+further south-west: a short steep fall from the tall stack, then one long coping line back past\n+the second stack. Neither picture shows any roof over that coping.\n+**What is invented.** What lies behind the coping: the fall's pitch (the street's own 61.2\n+degrees, the plainest choice; the plate's coping drops in about one column just behind the stack,\n+which a fall nearer 75 degrees would match better), the deck (flat, falling a quarter inch to the\n+foot to the rear wall, laid in the roof's slate where a tin deck is likelier; no picture sees it),\n+and the parapet's head running on 0.1 m behind the ridge. The rendered fall spreads over x 528-533\n+px where the plate's drops at x 527-528.\n+**Not changed here.** The plate and the print both step the flank down at the block's rear wall to\n+a lower wall head of about 8.6 m over the brick range; the build carries the range at 11.4 m (T-3077).\n+**How to resolve:** a view of the roof from above or behind (an aerial, a section, the 1965 HABS\n+photograph that T-3052 is to find), or T-3052's solved camera on the Chicagology print.\n+**Ticket:** T-3063 (piece 2 of T-3051).\n+**Review:** `data/reference_views/coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie/inland_architect_plate.match.json`.\n+**Recorded:** 2026-10-23 (T-3063)."},{"sha":"2acfe3e6eee50db2eade01d1b2da86ebf8eee9ce","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/README.md","status":"added","additions":89,"deletions":0,"changes":89,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2FREADME.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2FREADME.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2FREADME.md?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@\n+# Glessner's roof covering: red tile, and why every print reads it grey (T-3025, piece 3 of T-2854)\n+\n+Three Glessner match records carried one open item between them: the roofs, the stable\n+cupola's pyramid included, read slate-grey in the prints where the model lays red tile\n+house-wide (`habs-01-northwest`, `habs-15-stable-detail`, `cornell-northwest-west-windows`).\n+The ticket asks what the roof was laid in, from a contract, a specification, a description or\n+a colour view, and for a ruling.\n+\n+**Acceptance, stated before the work:** the covering is ruled on a written source that names\n+it, every match-record item that reads the covering from a print is closed on that ruling with\n+its reason, and the record is rebaked only if the ruling changes the covering.\n+\n+## 1. What the roof was laid in\n+\n+Two sources name it, and they are independent in kind.\n+\n+- **The owner's description of the house as built.** *\"The roofs are of red baked tiles,\n+  unglazed, the outside walls on the streets are of Wellesley granite, and all walls are lined\n+  with hollow brick\"* (J. J. Glessner, *The Story of a House*, March 1923;\n+  `glessner_story_of_a_house_1923`). Re-read for this ticket in the HABS transcription,\n+  `prairie_1904_v1/research/public/glessner-habs-data.pdf`, data p. 13 (PDF p. 14). He is\n+  describing construction (the granite, the hollow-brick lining), so it carries back to 1887\n+  and forward to 1904.\n+- **A physical survey.** *\"Roof surfaces are covered with terracotta, tar covered tiles, six\n+  inches wide with five inches of their length exposed\"* (HABS IL-1015 data, p. 21, 1963;\n+  `habs_glessner_house_il_1015_data_pages`). The surveyors were on the house: what lay under\n+  the tar was terracotta, so slate is excluded as a covering for any date the 1963 tiles were\n+  already on the roof.\n+\n+No contract or specification was found in the library, and no colour view of the house before\n+1904 is known to it. The 2024 colour photographs (`wlemay_glessner_courtyard_2024_*`) show\n+modern fabric and are kept out of the ruling.\n+\n+**Ruling: red baked, unglazed terracotta tile, house-wide, the cupola's pyramid included.** The\n+record already says so (`roof_covering`, `terracotta_tile`, attested on both sources), so\n+nothing moves and nothing is rebaked. The ruling is written on the three match records and here, not appended to the record's `roof_covering` note: that note is part of the light derivative's staleness hash (`validate.py --stale` reads it stale with one sentence added), so a prose-only change there would cost a bake. Glessner says \"the roofs\", HABS \"roof surfaces\", and\n+neither excepts the cupola. The c. 1887 Cornell print lays its pyramid in the same small\n+coursed units as the main roofs. The only exception either names is the hall bow, which is\n+copper and modelled copper.\n+\n+## 2. Why every print reads it grey\n+\n+Every picture of the house in the library is monochrome, and none of them can say what colour\n+a surface was (`data/reference_views/README.md`: colour in a monochrome print is `not shown`).\n+They fall into two groups:\n+\n+- **The 1963 and 1965 HABS prints** (photographs 1, 13-17) show the tiles under the tar HABS\n+  recorded that year. Their dark grey is the tar's.\n+- **The 1887-1888 prints** (the Cornell print, Taylor 2135, the *Inland Architect* plate) were\n+  made on dry plates, which before panchromatic emulsions recorded mostly blue and green light.\n+  A red surface records dark on them. This is the general behaviour of the period's plates, not\n+  a reading of these particular plates, so it is reasoning and is cited to nothing.\n+\n+`stable-roof-cornell.jpg` shows this. On the left is the Cornell print's stable roof between\n+the cupola and the north gable. In the middle is the render of the same plane through the same\n+solved camera, in the record's red tile. On the right is that render reduced to its luminance.\n+The red tile reads as a slate-grey roof darker than the granite, the same impression the\n+item recorded. A grey roof in a monochrome print is what this roof would look like whether it\n+was red or slate. It therefore cannot overrule the two written sources.\n+\n+One residual is recorded rather than used. The print's roof reads a little lighter against\n+its granite than the luminance render does. A roof slope and a wall face take different light,\n+and more so under the print's overcast sky. The emulsion's response is also not modelled. A\n+roof-to-wall tone ratio therefore measures the light as much as the colour, and it decides\n+nothing here.\n+\n+## 3. A finding on the module, not the material: a new ticket\n+\n+The Cornell print resolves the stable roof's courses. With the print and the render sharing one\n+camera, the same pixel columns cross the same plane in both, so the ratio of their course\n+periods is the print's course in units of the render's 5 in:\n+\n+    python3 docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/read_courses.py\n+\n+| columns | print period | render period | ratio | print course |\n+|---|---|---|---|---|\n+| 1000-1030 | 4.38 px | 3.40 px | 1.286 | 6.43 in |\n+| 1040-1080 | 4.45 px | 3.54 px | 1.257 | 6.28 in |\n+| 1090-1120 | 4.81 px | 3.67 px | 1.310 | 6.55 in |\n+| **mean** | | | **1.284** | **6.42 in** |\n+\n+(`readings.json`.) So the c. 1887 roof reads about 6.4 in to the course, where the model lays\n+HABS's 1963 5 in (L-glessner-roof-tiles-2203, which carries the 1963 module back to 1904 as\n+inferred and names \"a calibrated roof close-up\" as the way to settle it). The reading does not\n+separate tile from slate: a 16 in slate at a 3 in headlap also shows about 6.5 in. The material\n+ruling stands on section 1, and the module question is filed as its own ticket. It needs the\n+render's course measured at a resolution where the texture is not near its sampling limit\n+(3.4-3.7 px here), a second picture, and a look at whether the roof was relaid between 1887 and\n+1963."},{"sha":"4d2a4cfb280d139c061ad7f6bcfc0391cd2a0252","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/read_courses.py","status":"added","additions":57,"deletions":0,"changes":57,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fread_courses.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fread_courses.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fread_courses.py?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Count the stable roof's courses in the Cornell c. 1887 print against the render (T-3025).\n+\n+The print and the render on the committed side-by-side share one solved camera, so the same\n+pixel column crosses the same roof plane in both. The vertical period of the courses is read\n+per column with a Hann-windowed FFT and the power summed over a band of columns (the phase of\n+the courses drifts across a band, the period does not). The render lays courses at the record's\n+5 in exposure (masonry_house_v4_materials.py, 16 rows of 5 in), so the ratio of the two periods\n+is the print's exposure in units of 5 in.\n+\n+    python3 docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/read_courses.py\n+\"\"\"\n+import json\n+import pathlib\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+from PIL import Image\n+\n+ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n+SBS = ROOT / \"docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/glessner_house/cornell-northwest-west-windows-side-by-side.jpg\"\n+PHOTO_W = 1800                       # each half of the side-by-side, native pixels\n+ROWS = {\"print\": (300, 450), \"render\": (310, 460)}  # inside the roof field on both halves\n+BANDS = [(1000, 1030), (1040, 1080), (1090, 1120)]  # columns between the cupola and the gable\n+EXPOSURE_IN = 5.0                    # the render's course, from the record (HABS data p. 21)\n+\n+\n+def period(img, x0, x1, y0, y1, xo):\n+    power = None\n+    for x in range(x0, x1):\n+        col = img[y0:y1, x + xo].copy()\n+        col -= col.mean()\n+        col *= np.hanning(len(col))\n+        p = np.abs(np.fft.rfft(col, n=1024)) ** 2\n+        power = p if power is None else power + p\n+    f = np.fft.rfftfreq(1024)\n+    band = (f > 1 / 12) & (f < 1 / 2.5)\n+    return float(1 / f[np.argmax(power * band)])\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    img = np.asarray(Image.open(SBS).convert(\"L\"), float)\n+    off = img.shape[1] - PHOTO_W\n+    rows = []\n+    for x0, x1 in BANDS:\n+        pp = period(img, x0, x1, *ROWS[\"print\"], 0)\n+        pr = period(img, x0, x1, *ROWS[\"render\"], off)\n+        rows.append({\"columns\": [x0, x1], \"print_px\": round(pp, 2), \"render_px\": round(pr, 2),\n+                     \"ratio\": round(pp / pr, 3), \"print_exposure_in\": round(EXPOSURE_IN * pp / pr, 2)})\n+    ratios = [r[\"ratio\"] for r in rows]\n+    out = {\"side_by_side\": str(SBS.relative_to(ROOT)), \"bands\": rows,\n+           \"mean_ratio\": round(sum(ratios) / len(ratios), 3),\n+           \"print_exposure_in\": round(EXPOSURE_IN * sum(ratios) / len(ratios), 2)}\n+    print(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    main()"},{"sha":"8f6a92cf15799cb3bea4ca5fa7fafc2d46a26637","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/readings.json","status":"added","additions":37,"deletions":0,"changes":37,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Freadings.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Freadings.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Freadings.json?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+{\n+ \"side_by_side\": \"docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/glessner_house/cornell-northwest-west-windows-side-by-side.jpg\",\n+ \"bands\": [\n+  {\n+   \"columns\": [\n+    1000,\n+    1030\n+   ],\n+   \"print_px\": 4.38,\n+   \"render_px\": 3.4,\n+   \"ratio\": 1.286,\n+   \"print_exposure_in\": 6.43\n+  },\n+  {\n+   \"columns\": [\n+    1040,\n+    1080\n+   ],\n+   \"print_px\": 4.45,\n+   \"render_px\": 3.54,\n+   \"ratio\": 1.257,\n+   \"print_exposure_in\": 6.28\n+  },\n+  {\n+   \"columns\": [\n+    1090,\n+    1120\n+   ],\n+   \"print_px\": 4.81,\n+   \"render_px\": 3.67,\n+   \"ratio\": 1.31,\n+   \"print_exposure_in\": 6.55\n+  }\n+ ],\n+ \"mean_ratio\": 1.284,\n+ \"print_exposure_in\": 6.42\n+}"},{"sha":"661422000238771ca2d41000de423abd2b482ef2","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/RESEARCH/glessner-roof-covering-T-3025/stable-roof-cornell.jpg","status":"added","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fstable-roof-cornell.jpg","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fstable-roof-cornell.jpg","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fglessner-roof-covering-T-3025%2Fstable-roof-cornell.jpg?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854"},{"sha":"a7583f7e63d96dc5698cb3b10fc47944a80209e7","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie/inland_architect_plate-side-by-side.jpg","status":"modified","additions":0,"deletions":0,"changes":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fphoto-match%2Fcoleman_ames_house_1811_prairie%2Finland_architect_plate-side-by-side.jpg","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fphoto-match%2Fcoleman_ames_house_1811_prairie%2Finland_architect_plate-side-by-side.jpg","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2FRESEARCH%2Fphoto-match%2Fcoleman_ames_house_1811_prairie%2Finland_architect_plate-side-by-side.jpg?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854"},{"sha":"2469f8e1174110d69ea890a5104d4fcd6bacbd5d","filename":"chicago/4d/docs/measurements/source_use_coverage.md","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changes":2,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2Fmeasurements%2Fsource_use_coverage.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2Fmeasurements%2Fsource_use_coverage.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdocs%2Fmeasurements%2Fsource_use_coverage.md?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ Generated by `tools/compile_source_use.py`; no timestamps.\n | flora | 11 | 11 | 0 |\n | households | 2086 | 1457 | 0 |\n | jaunt claims | 33 | 33 | 0 |\n-| liberties (structured citations) | 702 | 0 | 0 |\n+| liberties (structured citations) | 703 | 0 | 0 |\n | loading facts | 50 | 50 | 0 |\n | people | 3878 | 1655 | 0 |\n | railway | 1 | 1 | 0 |"},{"sha":"f66e212d43918423b4941a8ecdbd17c7ec2da02e","filename":"chicago/4d/generators/archetypes/k01_frontage.py","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1,"changes":3,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage.py?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -2845,7 +2845,8 @@ def roof(self):\n                                   \"lower_rise_m\": m[\"lower_rise_m\"], \"curb_datum_m\": m[\"curb_m\"]} if m else {}),\n                               **({\"ridge_back_m\": gb[\"ridge_back_m\"], \"back_pitch_deg\": gb[\"back_pitch_deg\"],\n                                   \"parapets\": {k_: e[\"style\"] for k_, e in gb[\"ends\"].items()},\n-                                  \"parapet_top_m\": round(yr + gb[\"top_above_ridge_m\"], 4)} if gb else {}),\n+                                  \"parapet_top_m\": round(yr + gb[\"top_above_ridge_m\"], 4),\n+                                  **({\"rear_fall\": gb[\"rear_fall\"]} if gb.get(\"rear_fall\") else {})} if gb else {}),\n                               \"eave_datum_m\": E, \"ridge_datum_m\": yr, \"construction\": \"k05\",\n                               \"fascia_depth_m\": f, \"chimneys\": len(p.chimneys),\n                               **({\"covering\": k[\"covering\"], \"flashing\": k[\"flashing\"]} if k else {}),"},{"sha":"a1facca3749f4112813e7b45ad3d4980cbfb090f","filename":"chicago/4d/generators/archetypes/k01_frontage_params.py","status":"modified","additions":44,"deletions":2,"changes":46,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage_params.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage_params.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_frontage_params.py?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -466,6 +466,12 @@ def _flat_roof(depth: float, eave: float, pitch: float, overhang: float) -> dict\n GABLE_PARAPETS = (\"stepped\", \"coped\")\n \n \n+def _gable_top_half() -> float:\n+    \"\"\"The parapet's level head either side of the ridge (k01_gable_roof.TOP_HALF_M).\"\"\"\n+    from . import k01_gable_roof\n+    return k01_gable_roof.TOP_HALF_M\n+\n+\n def _gable_roof(g: dict, depth: float, width: float, eave: float, pitch: float, side_wall: float,\n                 overhang: float = 0.0) -> dict:\n     \"\"\"The numbers a K01 gable roof is built to (T-2459): the ridge runs along the street\n@@ -484,7 +490,16 @@ def _gable_roof(g: dict, depth: float, width: float, eave: float, pitch: float,\n     faces at roof_pitch_deg from the same eave, so its street face is the gable's own street\n     plane; `apex_v_m`, where a picture puts its apex, pitches its two end faces to it. The gable's attic\n     then starts at `attic_from_m`, inside the hip's south face, and only the high-v (`north`)\n-    wall is carried up as a parapet: the low-v wall is under the hip's end.\"\"\"\n+    wall is carried up as a parapet: the low-v wall is under the hip's end.\n+\n+    T-3063: `rear_fall` lets the rear slope fall steeply from the ridge, at its `pitch_deg`,\n+    to a FLAT DECK that runs to the rear wall, and the coped parapet over it fall with it to a\n+    LEVEL wall head, its coping's top at `wall_head_m`, the deck K05's upstand under the\n+    parapet's slab (1811's south\n+    wall behind its tall stack: both its pictures draw the coping level at about 10.95 m from\n+    just behind the stack to the block's rear wall, with no roof showing over it, where a rear\n+    slope falling to the rear eave stands it 0.5-1.4 m higher there). `head_back_m` is how far\n+    the parapet's level head runs on behind the ridge before it falls. Coped ends only.\"\"\"\n     if not g:\n         raise ParamError(\"a gable K01 roof names its gable_roof: ridge_back_m and the two ends\")\n     k5 = json.loads((ROOT / \"data\" / \"components\" / \"prairie_1904\" / \"k05_roofs.json\").read_text())\n@@ -518,6 +533,33 @@ def _gable_roof(g: dict, depth: float, width: float, eave: float, pitch: float,\n     top = float(g.get(\"top_above_ridge_m\", pp[\"top_above_ridge_m\"]))\n     if not pp[\"upstand_min_m\"] <= top <= 1.5:\n         raise ParamError(f\"gable_roof.top_above_ridge_m: {pp['upstand_min_m']}-1.5 m\")\n+    fall = {}\n+    rf = g.get(\"rear_fall\")\n+    if rf:\n+        if any(e[\"style\"] != \"coped\" for e in out.values()):\n+            raise ParamError(\"gable_roof.rear_fall: only a coped parapet runs level over a deck\")\n+        head, fp = float(rf[\"wall_head_m\"]), float(rf[\"pitch_deg\"])\n+        # how far the parapet's level head runs on behind the ridge before it falls (the\n+        # coped head's own half, unless a picture sees the fall start nearer the ridge)\n+        hb = float(rf.get(\"head_back_m\", _gable_top_half()))\n+        if not 0.05 <= hb <= _gable_top_half():\n+            raise ParamError(f\"gable_roof.rear_fall.head_back_m {hb}: 0.05-{_gable_top_half()} m\")\n+        if not back_deg + 15.0 <= fp <= 75.0:\n+            raise ParamError(f\"gable_roof.rear_fall.pitch_deg {fp}: from the plain rear slope's \"\n+                             f\"{back_deg:.1f} + 15 to 75 deg\")\n+        # the wall head is the coping's top, as a picture reads it; the parapet's slab stops a\n+        # coping under it, and the deck K05's least upstand under that\n+        up, ridge = float(pp[\"upstand_min_m\"]), eave + rise\n+        deck = head - float(cp[\"thickness_m\"]) - up\n+        run = (ridge - deck) / math.tan(math.radians(fp))\n+        # the deck stands over the front eave and under the ridge, and the fall is long enough\n+        # that the parapet's level head over the ridge stays over the covering behind it\n+        if not (eave + 0.5 <= deck and run >= hb + 0.05 and run <= depth - r - 1.0):\n+            raise ParamError(f\"gable_roof.rear_fall.wall_head_m {head}: its deck {deck:.3f} m must stand \"\n+                             f\"0.5 m over the eave {eave} and fall from the ridge {ridge:.3f} m over \"\n+                             f\"{hb + 0.05:.2f} m to 1 m short of the rear wall (it falls {run:.2f})\")\n+        fall = {\"rear_fall\": {\"wall_head_m\": head, \"pitch_deg\": fp, \"head_back_m\": hb, \"deck_m\": round(deck, 4),\n+                              \"deck_from_m\": round(depth - r - run, 4)}}\n     hip = {}\n     if hm:\n         vm, va = float(hm[\"v_m\"]), float(hm[\"attic_from_m\"])\n@@ -551,7 +593,7 @@ def _gable_roof(g: dict, depth: float, width: float, eave: float, pitch: float,\n                             \"apex_v_m\": av, \"end_pitch_deg\": {\"south\": round(math.degrees(math.atan(tn)), 4),\n                                                              \"north\": round(math.degrees(math.atan(ts)), 4)}}}\n     return {\"ridge_back_m\": r, \"ridge_m\": round(eave + rise, 4), \"back_pitch_deg\": round(back_deg, 4),\n-            **hip, \"ends\": out, \"parapet_m\": side_wall, \"upstand_m\": float(pp[\"upstand_min_m\"]),\n+            **hip, **fall, \"ends\": out, \"parapet_m\": side_wall, \"upstand_m\": float(pp[\"upstand_min_m\"]),\n             \"top_above_ridge_m\": top, \"coping_m\": float(cp[\"thickness_m\"]), \"drip_m\": float(cp[\"drip_m\"])}\n \n "},{"sha":"dc78bceccbb935eb96509b7fcd8743f3631f9cf0","filename":"chicago/4d/generators/archetypes/k01_gable_roof.py","status":"modified","additions":23,"deletions":4,"changes":27,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_gable_roof.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_gable_roof.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fgenerators%2Farchetypes%2Fk01_gable_roof.py?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -26,6 +26,10 @@\n T-3050: `hip_mass` adds a K05 hip over the low-v end of the block (1811 Prairie's tall hipped\n roof over its bay, the 1888 plate), its street face in the attic's street plane; the attic\n then starts inside it and only the high-v wall is a parapet.\n+\n+T-3063: `rear_fall` drops the rear slope steeply from the ridge to a flat DECK running to the\n+rear wall, and the coped parapet over it falls with it to a level wall head (1811 Prairie's\n+south wall behind its tall stack, level in the 1888 plate and the Chicagology print).\n \"\"\"\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n@@ -38,15 +42,24 @@\n # along the parapet's edges into a zero-area sliver (check_roof_kit's degenerate rule): 5 mm\n # behind it, nothing is coplanar and nothing a visitor can see has moved.\n FRONT_SET_M = 0.005\n+# T-3063: a rear fall's deck falls to the rear wall a quarter inch to the foot, a tin deck's\n+# usual fall, so it sheds water and its covering has an up-slope to course along\n+DECK_FALL = 1.0 / 48.0\n \n \n def line(style: str, steps: int, D: float, xr: float, E: float, tf: float, tb: float,\n-         up: float, top: float, th: float = TOP_HALF_M) -> list:\n+         up: float, top: float, th: float = TOP_HALF_M, fall: dict | None = None) -> list:\n     \"\"\"The parapet's top line in (u, y) from the rear wall's plane (u 0) to the front's (u D):\n     every point clears the covering under it by `up`; its head, about the ridge at u `xr`,\n-    stands level at `top`.\"\"\"\n+    stands level at `top`. T-3063: over a rear fall's deck (`fall`, coped only) the line runs\n+    level at the deck + `up` from the rear wall to where the fall meets the deck, and climbs\n+    from there to the head's rear end, `head_back_m` behind the ridge: steeper than the fall,\n+    so it clears it all the way.\"\"\"\n     def roof(x):\n         return E + min((D - x) * tf, x * tb)\n+    if style == \"coped\" and fall:\n+        y0 = fall[\"deck_m\"] + up\n+        return [(0.0, y0), (fall[\"deck_from_m\"], y0), (xr - fall[\"head_back_m\"], top), (xr + th, top), (D, E + up)]\n     if style == \"coped\":\n         return [(0.0, E + up), (xr - th, top), (xr + th, top), (D, E + up)]\n     pts = []\n@@ -90,7 +103,12 @@ def elements(p, k5, E: float, o: float, f: float):\n     # T-3050: under a hipped mass the attic starts inside the hip, at `attic_from_m`\n     hm = g.get(\"hip_mass\")\n     z1 = -hm[\"attic_from_m\"] if hm else 0.0\n-    attic = k5.extrude([(-o, hs), (D + o, hs), (D + o, hef), (xr, yr), (-o, her)], -W, z1, P,\n+    rf = g.get(\"rear_fall\")\n+    # T-3063: behind a rear fall the attic's back is the fall down to the deck, level to the\n+    # rear wall's plane, where the deck stops: no eave overhangs it\n+    outline = ([(0.0, hs), (D + o, hs), (D + o, hef), (xr, yr), (rf[\"deck_from_m\"], rf[\"deck_m\"]),\n+                (0.0, rf[\"deck_m\"] - rf[\"deck_from_m\"] * DECK_FALL)] if rf else [(-o, hs), (D + o, hs), (D + o, hef), (xr, yr), (-o, her)])\n+    attic = k5.extrude(outline, -W, z1, P,\n                        k5.by_edge(\"covering\", \"soffit\", \"fascia\"), \"fascia\", \"fascia\")\n     tw, up = g[\"parapet_m\"], g[\"upstand_m\"]\n     top = yr + g[\"top_above_ridge_m\"]\n@@ -99,7 +117,8 @@ def elements(p, k5, E: float, o: float, f: float):\n         if side not in g[\"ends\"]:\n             continue\n         e = g[\"ends\"][side]\n-        ln = [(min(x, D - FRONT_SET_M), y) for x, y in line(e[\"style\"], e.get(\"steps\", 0), D, xr, E, tf, tb, up, top)]\n+        ln = [(min(x, D - FRONT_SET_M), y)\n+              for x, y in line(e[\"style\"], e.get(\"steps\", 0), D, xr, E, tf, tb, up, top, fall=rf)]\n         # each parapet stands on its wall from the soffit up, the wall's top under the eave\n         solids += k5.parapet_element({}, ln, (c0, c1), \"z\", tw, hs, g[\"coping_m\"], g[\"drip_m\"], 0.0, 0.0)\n         lines[side] = [[round(a, 4), round(b, 4)] for a, b in ln]"},{"sha":"b6e878e5a7e23610b5b34a4b1af4729a017245f7","filename":"chicago/4d/tools/check.sh","status":"modified","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changes":8,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fcheck.sh","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fcheck.sh","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fcheck.sh?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -1020,6 +1020,14 @@ step \"a K01 frontage carries a K08 tower past its eave, closed above the wall he\n step \"a K01 rear wing takes a slated hip or gable, its junction with the host closed above the host's top (T-2841)\" \\\n   python3 tools/test_k01_wing_roof.py\n \n+# T-3063. ...and a K01 gable roof's rear slope falls steeply to a flat deck under a level\n+# coped wall head (1811 Prairie's south wall behind its tall stack, level in both its\n+# pictures): the deck under the coping, the line level to the fall's foot and clear of the\n+# covering everywhere, 1811 built so, the plain coped line unchanged, and a fall over\n+# stepped ends, out of its pitch range, over the ridge or with too long a head refused.\n+step \"a K01 gable roof's rear slope falls to a deck under a level coped wall head (T-3063)\" \\\n+  python3 tools/test_k01_rear_fall.py\n+\n # T-2842. ...and a K08 tower stands on a K01 rear wing's wall, past the wing's own eave (the\n # kit piece 1801 Prairie's north-east turret on its east range needs). Built on 1604's\n # brick range under its flat deck and on 1811 as all-stone with its rear section hipped in"},{"sha":"5a905b96682896b002cf62fccc33c21a45d80cea","filename":"chicago/4d/tools/step_isolation.json","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changes":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fstep_isolation.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fstep_isolation.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Fstep_isolation.json?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -5770,6 +5770,10 @@\n       \"wrote\": [],\n       \"wrote_ignored\": []\n     },\n+    \"tools/test_k01_rear_fall.py\": {\n+      \"wrote\": [],\n+      \"wrote_ignored\": []\n+    },\n     \"tools/test_k01_round_corner.py\": {\n       \"wrote\": [],\n       \"wrote_ignored\": []"},{"sha":"72afbee7f74fe1a8a875825bdc07bef49750820d","filename":"chicago/4d/tools/test_k01_rear_fall.py","status":"added","additions":120,"deletions":0,"changes":120,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Ftest_k01_rear_fall.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Ftest_k01_rear_fall.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Ftools%2Ftest_k01_rear_fall.py?ref=e3baf9323b06a1fb66d3a506b7430f9f10cd7854","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"T-3063: a K01 gable roof's rear slope may fall steeply to a flat deck under a level coping.\n+\n+1811 Prairie's south wall behind its tall stack: the 1888 plate and the Chicagology print both\n+draw its coping LEVEL at about 10.95 m back to the front block's rear wall, with no roof over\n+it, where K01's coped parapet followed the rear slope down to the rear eave. The record names\n+`gable_roof.rear_fall` (wall_head_m, pitch_deg, head_back_m); this holds the kit to it:\n+\n+  * resolved: the deck stands a coping and K05's upstand under the wall head, and the fall\n+    meets it where the fall's pitch from the ridge puts it;\n+  * the line: level at the wall head's slab from the rear wall to the fall's foot, the head\n+    `head_back_m` behind the ridge, and every point clearing the covering under it by the\n+    upstand; the 1811 build carries that line;\n+  * as-was: without rear_fall the coped line is T-2459's, point for point;\n+  * refused: a rear fall over stepped ends, a fall shallower than the plain rear slope + 15\n+    or steeper than 75 degrees, a deck over the ridge, a head run out of range.\n+\n+    python3 tools/test_k01_rear_fall.py\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import copy\n+import json\n+import math\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n+sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"generators\"))\n+\n+from archetypes import k01_frontage as K1  # noqa: E402\n+from archetypes import k01_frontage_params as KP  # noqa: E402\n+from archetypes import k01_gable_roof as KG  # noqa: E402\n+\n+SID = \"coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie\"\n+failures = []\n+\n+\n+def check(ok, what):\n+    print((\"ok   \" if ok else \"FAIL \") + what)\n+    if not ok:\n+        failures.append(what)\n+\n+\n+def record():\n+    return json.loads((ROOT / \"data\" / \"structures\" / f\"{SID}.json\").read_text())\n+\n+\n+def params(st):\n+    ph = next(p for p in st[\"phases\"] if \"form\" in p)\n+    return KP.from_phase(ph, st)\n+\n+\n+def refused(change, what):\n+    st = record()\n+    change(st[\"phases\"][0][\"form\"][\"gable_roof\"][\"value\"])\n+    try:\n+        params(st)\n+    except KP.ParamError as e:\n+        check(True, f\"refused: {what} ({str(e)[:90]})\")\n+        return\n+    check(False, f\"refused: {what}\")\n+\n+\n+p = params(record())\n+g, rf = p.gable, p.gable[\"rear_fall\"]\n+up, cop = g[\"upstand_m\"], g[\"coping_m\"]\n+check(abs(rf[\"deck_m\"] - (rf[\"wall_head_m\"] - cop - up)) < 1e-6,\n+      f\"the deck {rf['deck_m']} m stands a coping and the upstand under the {rf['wall_head_m']} m wall head\")\n+xr = p.depth_m - g[\"ridge_back_m\"]\n+run = (g[\"ridge_m\"] - rf[\"deck_m\"]) / math.tan(math.radians(rf[\"pitch_deg\"]))\n+check(abs(rf[\"deck_from_m\"] - (xr - run)) < 1e-3,\n+      f\"the fall meets the deck {rf['deck_from_m']} m from the rear wall, {run:.2f} m behind the ridge\")\n+\n+tf = math.tan(math.radians(p.roof_pitch_deg))\n+top = g[\"ridge_m\"] + g[\"top_above_ridge_m\"]\n+E = g[\"ridge_m\"] - g[\"ridge_back_m\"] * tf\n+ln = KG.line(\"coped\", 0, p.depth_m, xr, E, tf, math.tan(math.radians(g[\"back_pitch_deg\"])), up, top, fall=rf)\n+y0 = rf[\"deck_m\"] + up\n+check(ln[0] == (0.0, y0) and ln[1] == (rf[\"deck_from_m\"], y0),\n+      f\"the line runs level at {y0:.3f} m (the coping's top {y0 + cop:.2f}) to the fall's foot\")\n+check(abs(ln[2][0] - (xr - rf[\"head_back_m\"])) < 1e-9 and ln[2][1] == top,\n+      f\"its head starts {rf['head_back_m']} m behind the ridge at {top:.3f} m\")\n+\n+\n+def covering(x):\n+    \"\"\"The attic's top over u x: the street slope, the fall and the deck.\"\"\"\n+    if x >= xr:\n+        return E + (p.depth_m - x) * tf\n+    return max(rf[\"deck_m\"], g[\"ridge_m\"] - (xr - x) * math.tan(math.radians(rf[\"pitch_deg\"])))\n+\n+\n+def at(x):\n+    for (a, ya), (b, yb) in zip(ln, ln[1:]):\n+        if a - 1e-9 <= x <= b + 1e-9:\n+            return ya if b == a else ya + (yb - ya) * (x - a) / (b - a)\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+worst = min(at(x) - covering(x) for x in [i * p.depth_m / 400 for i in range(401)])\n+check(worst >= up - 1e-6, f\"every point of the line clears the covering by the {up} m upstand (least {worst:.3f})\")\n+\n+a = K1.build(p, SID)\n+built = a.gable_roof[\"parapet_lines\"][\"north\"]\n+check(built[0] == [0.0, round(y0, 4)] and built[1][1] == round(y0, 4),\n+      f\"1811's south parapet is built level at {y0:.3f} m from its rear wall\")\n+\n+old = KG.line(\"coped\", 0, 7.57, 6.17, 9.14, tf, 0.41, 0.3, 11.99)\n+check(old == [(0.0, 9.14 + 0.3), (6.17 - KG.TOP_HALF_M, 11.99), (6.17 + KG.TOP_HALF_M, 11.99), (7.57, 9.14 + 0.3)],\n+      \"without a rear fall the coped line is T-2459's, point for point\")\n+\n+refused(lambda v: v[\"ends\"][\"north\"].update({\"style\": \"stepped\", \"steps\": 3}), \"a rear fall over stepped ends\")\n+refused(lambda v: v[\"rear_fall\"].update({\"pitch_deg\": 30.0}), \"a fall under the plain rear slope + 15 degrees\")\n+refused(lambda v: v[\"rear_fall\"].update({\"pitch_deg\": 80.0}), \"a fall steeper than 75 degrees\")\n+refused(lambda v: v[\"rear_fall\"].update({\"wall_head_m\": 12.5}), \"a deck over the ridge\")\n+refused(lambda v: v[\"rear_fall\"].update({\"head_back_m\": 0.6}), \"a head run past K01's coped head\")\n+\n+print(f\"\\n{len(failures)} failure(s)\")\n+sys.exit(1 if failures else 0)"}]}